{{also|chock-a-block|chock a block}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|chock-a-block}}
* {{l|en|chock a block}}
* {{l|en|choc-a-bloc}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|chock}} + {{m|en|-a-}} + {{m|en|block}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈt͡ʃɒkəˌblɒk/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-chockablock.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} (of a ship's [[hoist]]ing [[tackle]]) Having the [[block]]s drawn close together so no further [[movement]] is possible, as when the tackle is [[haul]]ed to the utmost.
# {{lb|en|by extension}} [[jammed|Jammed]] [[tightly]] together; very [[crowded]]; completely [[filled]] or [[stuffed]].
#: ''Some of Sardinia's gorgeous seaside towns have lately been invaded by builders who erected '''chockablock''' housing that catered to middle-income tourists but threatened to spoil the landscape.''

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|chock}}
* {{l|en|chocka}}
* {{l|en|chocker}}
* {{l|en|chockers}}
* {{l|en|chokka}}

